    "--- \n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Document Pre-Processing, Sentence Indexing, and Boilerplate Filtering\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Item 1 Extraction and Pinned Segmentation (`relevance.segment_item1`)\n",
    "- 10-K Item 1 Business Description sections are isolated from full filings (median ~15,000 words per filing).\n",
    "- Uses the identical pinned `pysbd` (v0.3.4) segmenter as Task 2 to ensure sentence units are comparable between legislative evidence and corporate disclosures.\n",
    "- **Length Gate**: Sentences shorter than 30 characters (`keep_sentence`) are discarded to eliminate table residues, section headers (`\"Item 1. Business.\"`), and pagination fragments.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Cross-Firm Boilerplate Removal by Rule (`relevance.dedup_key`)\n",
    "- Rather than using black-box LLM filtering, boilerplate is detected deterministically:\n",
    "  1. Sentences are normalized: lowercased, digits collapsed to `#` (to match dates/dollar amounts), punctuation and whitespace stripped (`normalize_for_dedup`).\n",
    "  2. A stable SHA-1 hash key (`dedup_key`) is computed.\n",
    "  3. Any sentence template appearing in **$\ge 20$ distinct corporate filings** (e.g., standard safe-harbor statements, stock exchange listings) is filtered out."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstrating Boilerplate Normalization & Deduplication Hash from T3.X/relevance.py\n",
    "import hashlib\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "def normalize_for_dedup(sentence: str) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Canonical form for cross-document boilerplate detection.\"\"\"\n",
    "    s = sentence.lower()\n",
    "    s = re.sub(r\"\\d+\", \"#\", s)\n",
    "    s = re.sub(r\"[^a-z#]+\", \"\", s)\n",
    "    return s\n",
    "\n",
    "def dedup_key(sentence: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return hashlib.sha1(normalize_for_dedup(sentence).encode()).hexdigest()[:16]\n",
    "\n",
    "sample_1 = \"Our common stock is listed on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol XYZ.\"\n",
    "sample_2 = \"Our common stock is listed on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol ABC.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Sample 1 Hash:\", dedup_key(sample_1))\n",
    "print(\"Sample 2 Hash:\", dedup_key(sample_2))\n",
    "print(\"Identical boilerplate hash match:\", dedup_key(sample_1) == dedup_key(sample_2))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Dual-Instrument Measurement Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "To ensure construct validity without relying on a single model's inferences, two independent instruments are constructed:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instrument 1: The Deterministic Embedding Rail (`relevance.py`)\n",
    "- Embeds all 10-K sentences using `BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5` (CLS-pooled, L2-normalized float16 vectors).\n",
    "- Measures dense vector cosine similarity against the 111 policy topic centroids computed from congressional hearing evidence sentences.\n",
    "- 100% deterministic, zero LLM generation inference, perfectly reproducible.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instrument 2: 2-Pass Index-Cited LLM Tagging (`tagging.py`)\n",
    "- Evaluates 40-sentence blocks (`BLOCK_SENTENCES = 40`) with filing-global sentence numbers `[1] .. [40]`.\n",
    "- **Pass A (The Gate)**: The LLM rapidly filters the 111 topic labels down to a handful of candidate topic IDs matching the block (`GATE_MAX_NEW_TOKENS = 160`).\n",
    "- **Pass B (The Confirmation)**: The LLM reads candidate topics with full frozen definitions and outputs compact index-cited triples `[sentence_number, topic_id, direction]` where direction is `\"O\"` (Opportunity), `\"T\"` (Threat), or `\"N\"` (Neutral) (`CONFIRM_MAX_NEW_TOKENS = 512`).\n",
    "- **Index Grounding**: Uses sentence number citations rather than verbatim quotes, guaranteeing verifiable grounding."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. LLM Prompts & Exact Templates\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1. Pass A: Gate Screening Prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "**System Prompt:**\n",
    "> `You are an expert reader of corporate 10-K filings with a working knowledge of United States science and technology policy. You report only what the text states.`\n",
    "\n",
    "**User Prompt Template (`GATE_USER`):**\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Below are numbered consecutive sentences from the Business section (Item 1) of one company's 10-K annual report, followed by a list of policy topics drawn from congressional science-committee hearings.\n",
    "\n",
    "--- SENTENCES ---\n",
    "{numbered}\n",
    "--- END OF SENTENCES ---\n",
    "\n",
    "--- TOPICS ---\n",
    "{topics}\n",
    "--- END OF TOPICS ---\n",
    "\n",
    "A topic matches when at least one specific sentence describes a part of this company's business that falls in the topic's subject area — its products, services, technologies, inputs, customers, or the regulations it operates under. The sentence does not need to mention any law, agency, or hearing. Be generous: include plausible matches. Do not include a topic on the strength of generic statements that are not about this company's business.\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer with only a JSON list of the matching topic ids:\n",
    "[<topic id>, <topic id>]\n",
    "\n",
    "If no topic matches, answer [].\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "--- \n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.2. Pass B: Confirmation & Directional Tagging Prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "**System Prompt:**\n",
    "> `You are an expert reader of corporate 10-K filings with a working knowledge of United States science and technology policy. You report only what the text states.`\n",
    "\n",
    "**User Prompt Template (`CONFIRM_USER`):**\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Below are numbered sentences from the Business section (Item 1) of one company's 10-K annual report, and a list of policy topics with definitions.\n",
    "\n",
    "--- SENTENCES ---\n",
    "{numbered}\n",
    "--- END OF SENTENCES ---\n",
    "\n",
    "--- TOPICS ---\n",
    "{topics}\n",
    "--- END OF TOPICS ---\n",
    "\n",
    "Find every sentence that describes this company's business in a topic's subject area. The sentence does not need to mention a law, an agency, or a hearing. Skip generic statements that are not about this company. A sentence may match several topics.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each match, output one record: [sentence number, topic id, direction]. The direction is one letter:\n",
    "- \"O\" — the sentence presents it as growth, demand, funding, or an advantage for the company\n",
    "- \"T\" — the sentence presents it as a risk, cost, restriction, or competitive pressure\n",
    "- \"N\" — neither: the connection is stated without either\n",
    "\n",
    "Use only sentence numbers shown above and topic ids from the list.\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer with only a JSON list of records:\n",
    "[[<sentence number>, <topic id>, \"O\"]]\n",
    "\n",
    "If nothing matches, answer [].\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
