    "--- \n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Inference Optimization & Tag Parsing Safeguards\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Minimal Output Representations\n",
    "- Pass A outputs bare topic IDs (`[12, 45]`) rather than object wrappers, reducing decoding time to ~3.3s/block.\n",
    "- Pass B emits compact triples (`[sentence_idx, topic_id, "O"|"T"|"N"]`), keeping token consumption well below the 512-token budget ceiling.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Fault-Tolerant JSON Parsing (`tagging.py`)\n",
    "- Handles markdown code fences (````json ... ````) and cleans trailing truncated commas.\n",
    "- Validates sentence index boundaries (`1 <= idx <= n_sentences`), topic ID membership in the candidate set, and direction legend conformance (`O`, `T`, `N`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Demonstrating Triple Output Parsing and Validation from T3.X/tagging.py\n",
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_model_output = '[[14, 12, \"O\"], [18, 45, \"T\"]]'\n",
    "valid_topic_ids = {12, 45, 88}\n",
    "n_block_sentences = 40\n",
    "\n",
    "records = json.loads(raw_model_output)\n",
    "validated = []\n",
    "for r in records:\n",
    "    sent_idx, topic_id, direction = r\n",
    "    if 1 <= sent_idx <= n_block_sentences and topic_id in valid_topic_ids and direction in (\"O\", \"T\", \"N\"):\n",
    "        validated.append({\"sent_idx\": sent_idx, \"topic_id\": topic_id, \"direction\": direction})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Validated Tag Records:\", validated)\n"
   ]
